+++++From 4a25953cbdc15c82d7db85a99a9bf842899188bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+++++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+++++Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:47:57 -0500
+++++Subject: [PATCH] chat: add K2-Horizon workaround for reasoning-tag
+++++ auto-detection
+++++
+++++K2-Horizon's chat template picks its reasoning open/close tag based on
+++++the request's chat_template_kwargs.reasoning_effort ("high" ->
+++++"<ifm|think>", "medium" -> "<ifm|think_fast>", "low" ->
+++++"<ifm|think_faster>"). The diff-based autoparser renders the template
+++++once with a fixed set of probe kwargs and never observes this
+++++effort-conditional branch, so detection came back reasoning_mode::NONE
+++++entirely (confirmed live: /props reported chat_format "Content-only",
+++++reasoning_format "none") -- not a wrong guess, just nothing detected.
+++++
+++++Effect in production: the model's own thinking-close tag leaked
+++++verbatim into the API response's "content" field instead of being
+++++split into "reasoning_content" (e.g. content starting with the raw
+++++"</ifm|think_faster>" token). Initially suspected as the cause of a
+++++separate directory-name corruption bug; live testing showed the two
+++++are unrelated -- the corruption was actually a missing EOG-token
+++++registration (see the preceding commit) and persists/resolves
+++++independently of this tag leak.
+++++
+++++This fleet's own deployment pins reasoning_effort:"low" everywhere
+++++K2-Horizon runs (chosen over the default "high", which reproduced
+++++proper-noun garbling during its own chain-of-thought), so this
+++++workaround targets the "low" tag actually in use. The autoparser only
+++++supports one static start/end tag pair per template, not a per-request
+++++alternative set -- the other two tag variants are registered as
+++++preserved_tokens only, not as the parsed boundary, and this comment is
+++++repeated in the workaround itself so a future reasoning_effort change
+++++doesn't silently regress this.
+++++
+++++Verified live with a from-scratch local CPU build against the real
+++++deployed GGUF: the raw tag no longer appears in "content" for any case
+++++in the same test battery used for the preceding EOG-token commit.
+++++
