+diff --git a/fleet-patches/0065-vulkan-size-submit-batches-from-the-current-graph-s-.patch b/fleet-patches/0065-vulkan-size-submit-batches-from-the-current-graph-s-.patch
+new file mode 100644
+index 000000000..3ed430d08
+--- /dev/null
++++ b/fleet-patches/0065-vulkan-size-submit-batches-from-the-current-graph-s-.patch
+@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
++From b1ff71165c3ba895e6bf240db11f61f1df352ec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:45:55 -0500
++Subject: [PATCH] vulkan : size submit batches from the current graph's flops
++
++flops_per_submit was derived from the previous graph's total flops. The
++first large graph after a small one (a prompt ubatch after 1-token
++decode) got a tiny per-submit budget, so it submitted almost every node
++separately. On amdgpu that fills the 32-job scheduler queue, the submit
++ioctl blocks, and graph_compute turns synchronous -- which also stops
++pipeline parallelism across devices (~1.1 s stall on the first ubatch
++on gfx1151).
++
++Sum the current graph's flops in one pass before the submit loop and
++drop last_total_flops.
++
++Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
++---
++ ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-types.h |  1 -
++ ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp     | 13 +++++++++----
