++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 01:19:14 -0500
++Subject: [PATCH] vulkan : keep the flop-sized submits of a graph below the
++ kernel job queue
++
++A 512-token prompt ubatch of Qwen3.8-27B on the 8060S is ~22 TFLOP, so
++with the 200 GFLOP per-submit cap graph_compute issued ~110 submits.
++amdgpu queues 32 jobs per ring (sched_jobs); beyond that vkQueueSubmit
++blocks until the GPU catches up, so graph_compute returned only near the
++end of the graph and the host could not feed the next pipeline stage.
++
++Size the flop-based submits so a graph has at most 12 of them, except
++on the weak AMD GPUs whose lower cap exists to avoid the driver timeout.
++
++llama-bench, 8060S + 780M over RPC, 13/51 layers: pp2048 274 -> 294,
++pp8192 290 -> 316 t/s; single device unchanged (317/295).
++
++Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
